Subject: [PATCH 11232/11362] Memory index: the drift reminder names the index
 file that holds the line (REQ-INFRA-6976 D)

A demoted file's pointer lives in _index_<group>.md. The REQ-INFRA-6975
hook text still said "the MEMORY.md line", so an editor who appended to
a demoted file would have been sent to the wrong file. index_locations()
now maps a file to the index file that holds its line, and
expected_index_file() names where an unindexed file's line belongs. Both
are in the reminder. Also a both-caps test that makes the line-cap kept
slice load-bearing: the first mutation of that rule survived because it
deleted only half of it.

Proofs, synchronous: 20 of 21 RED in the first pass, then 3 of 3 RED in
the targeted pass (M03 in both forms, and the hook-location site); every
restore byte-identical by cmp; GREEN after each restore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
